  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting women&apos;s economic empowerment in Usulutan, El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This amendment provides ACOMUDT with an additional year and $140,960 to expand upon successful activities such as training its network of women members in Usulutn in women&apos;s rights and strengthening their women-led microenterprises to promote their economic independence. ACOMUDT will expand training on women&apos;s rights to five remote, relatively unconnected communities in three municipalities, increase its own administrative and financial capacity, and provide credit to additional women to create or consolidate their microenterprises.</narrative>
  </description>
